# Arbor investigation

This copy is r-lidar/arbor 1.1.2 (GPL-3). The product API is the R package. The C++ entry without R is `src/api/arbor.h`.

Three tracks, notes only until a track asks for code:

1. `notes/01-cpp.md` — map the engine and the public C++ surface
2. `notes/02-swift-api.md` — how a Swift API would call that C++
3. `notes/03-macos.md` — why the C++ misbehaves on macOS

- Record observed facts separately from guesses. Do not treat a hypothesis as a diagnosed bug.
- Do not edit `src/vendor/` unless a vendored bug is the task.
- Do not hand-edit `NAMESPACE` or `src/RcppExports.cpp`.
- Keep new notes and agent files out of the R tarball (`.Rbuildignore`).
- `USING_R` swaps `PointCloud` and pulls in Rcpp. A Swift or standalone build must not define it.
